# Project Coding Standards

- Follow Google-style open source engineering practices.
- Explain technical decisions in plain English before implementation details.
- Prioritize readability and developer experience over clever shortcuts.
- Remove dead or unused code instead of leaving it "just in case".
- Fix type errors directly; do not silence or bypass type checks.
- Identify potential risks in changes and propose actionable fixes.
- Follow the existing project structure and naming conventions.
- Keep outputs production-ready, with clear failure handling and validation.
